// Title: Potential RDP Session Hijacking Activity
// Sigma ID: 224f140f-3553-4cd1-af78-13d81bf9f7cc
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @juju4
// Date: 2022-12-27 | Modified: 2024-12-01
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects potential RDP Session Hijacking activity on Windows systems
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/Moti_B/status/909449115477659651
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_tscon_rdp_session_hijacking.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\tscon.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "tscon.exe") and (ProcessIntegrityLevel in~ ("System", "S-1-16-16384"))
